## Integer endpoint calculus and mandatory coordinate padding

S=2^768 rectangles have four integer endpoints divided by S in the order
(real_lo,real_hi,imag_lo,imag_hi). Real products take extrema over all four
corners. Complex products use ac-bd and ad+bc, then floor/ceiling division
by positive S. Signed exact Gaussian-integer multiplication swaps endpoints
where needed. All16 matrix entries, including identity phases, are retained.

At substep start h=k/8 the shifted waveform coefficients are exactly

    16h^2(1-h)^2, 32h(1-h)(1-2h),
    16-96h+96h^2, -32+64h, 16.

For A(z)=-i[K+a psi(h+z)P], all A_j are exact Gaussian rationals. The
code accumulates sparse left products with common denominator d and uses

    U_0=I, (m+1)U_(m+1)=sum_(j<=min(4,m)) A_j U_(m-j).

One outward division by d(m+1) follows the integer sum. Horner evaluation
at1/8 and chronological left multiplication enclose the exact truncated
product, by induction, including rounding. Legal amplitudes lie in[1/4,3/4]
and in particular are below1, so the accepted scalar majorant
7+32z+64z^2+128z^3+64z^4 applies. Its integral at1/4 is773/240<4; its
solution has value<81. Consequently a degree320 segment tail is bounded
by delta=81/2^321. Comparing192 approximate segments to exact unitary
segments gives the uniform endpoint error

    e0=384delta=31104/2^321.

The saved nominal rectangle encloses an exact truncated matrix Uhat with
||Uhat-U0||<=e0. The saved power encloses Dhat=Uhat^n with
||Dhat-D||<=eta_D=2ne0. This is qualified parent evidence, not a new power
calculation. A new endpoint rectangle encloses Fhat, ||Fhat-F||<=e0.

For G the interval product Uhat^dagger Fhat differs from the true product
by at most gamma=e0(1+e0)+e0. For y, Dhat^dagger Z differs from D^dagger Z
by at most eta_D, because the exact Z is unitary and its full analytic
enclosure is already in the root rectangle. Each normalized Pauli trace
error is bounded by the operator error: |Tr(PE)/4|<=||E||op. Thus the
program adds ceil(S gamma) or ceil(S eta_D) to each imaginary-coordinate
